       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. The single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this exposure the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThese are the options I can enter, depending on what you intend:\n\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory or analgesic use.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common, more conservative option.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day). This may be what was meant if the total daily dose was 1,600 mg.\n\nIf 1,600 mg was meant as the daily total, tell me the dose and frequency you want. For example, I could enter 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily. If you want a dose above the labeled maximum for a specific reason, please check it with pharmacy or the attending first. I can't enter it on the basis of an unverified approval."
      }
