       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1,600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and I can't verify the clinical justification from here.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the labeled maximum.\n- **A lower dose** such as 600 mg or 400 mg four times daily, if you prefer.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, you could:\n\n1. **Consult pharmacy or the attending.** They can review the indication and enter the order through whatever process your hospital uses for above-label dosing.\n2. **Consider alternatives.** If 3,200 mg/day of ibuprofen isn't enough, another agent or a multimodal regimen may work better than a higher NSAID dose. Pharmacy can help choose one.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter one of the in-range options now."
      }
